  "instructions": [
    "Combine rice flour, urad dal, and salt in a large bowl.",
    "Gradually add water and mix until a smooth batter forms.",
    "Add mirin-hon, yuzu juice, sugar, and active dry yeast to the batter and mix well.",
    "Cover the bowl with a damp cloth and let it rest for 4-5 hours at room temperature.",
    "After the fermentation process, add coconut oil and mix well.",
    "Heat a non-stick idli mold or a steamer basket with some water coming up to the bottom of the mold.",
    "Pour the batter into the mold and steam for 10-12 minutes or until the idlis are cooked through and crispy on the outside.",
    "Remove the idlis from the mold and serve hot with chopped cilantro and yuzu-cure if desired."
  ],
